meta {
  name: 53 Bulk Mark Returned Verified
  type: http
  seq: 53
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/bulk/mark-returned-verified
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "ids": ["{{sampleId}}"],
    "skipInvalid": true,
    "notes": "Sample is back in the lab and checked"
  }
}

tests {
  test("verified (or refused)", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 201, 422]);
  });
}

docs {
  Confirm that **Returned** samples are physically back and checked (Sample Search popup). Retrieve out
  of Returned is refused (`SAMPLE_RETRIEVE_BLOCKED_NOT_VERIFIED`) until this is done. Records who and
  when (`returnedVerifiedBy` / `returnedVerifiedAt`) and a history line. A sample can be verified once.
  Permission: the same as Return. All-or-nothing for the ids, unless `skipInvalid: true` (the Sample Search popup sends
  it): a sample that is no longer Returned, is already verified (someone else just did it) or whose order is cancelled is
  then left out and named in `skipped` while the others are verified. A missing id always fails the call.

  The popup sends ONLY the unverified rows of a section (a section can hold verified and unverified rows when its tests
  were returned separately), after showing the person which tests it will change.

  Errors (422): `SAMPLE_FLAG_NOT_ALLOWED` (not Returned, or already verified), `SAMPLE_ORDER_CANCELLED`.
}
